    "qualification": "Production build; 263 targeted lake checks and 98 graph/page checks passed, one declared skip, zero failures/leaks; 35 real Parquet/Iceberg E2Es passed without skips; 28 exact paired pages including scores and work counts."
  },
  "changes": [
    "Navigation cache entries retain a shared prefix plus borrowed suffixes. Cursor views compare complete logical keys without entry-wise expansion; identity scans validate only the final coordinate and materialize one required boundary.",
    "Sorted and incremental packing use compressed occupancy while preserving expanded hard limits, summary headroom and pending child locator reservations. Repair cannot over-merge small compressed siblings.",
    "Native ordered producers enable page-prefix encoding for serving, reverse and checkpoint forests. Old page formats and immutable roots remain readable; new builds and rewritten pages gain packing improvements.",
    "Pagination checks repeat identical cursor requests to verify physical reuse. Peak allocation, rather than historical speculative-resize rejection, qualifies successful bounded output."
  ],
